ife  at the time I was having this internal  debate with myself because I had seen a  medical professional and spoken to  another that it assured me that  everything was going to be okay now that  I look back that I was really  downplaying these symptoms and then  finally on March 1st 2020 I woke up and  I started feeling oddly normal I made  myself a cup of coffee i sat down on my  desk and I started working like I would  have any other day and then it was when  I made myself breakfast that I realized  if I had absolutely no taste and no  smile and that I hadn't had these two  senses since the day that I became ill  and then since I had been assured and  reassured by doctors that I don't have  any Korona symptoms and I was feeling  better I just returned to life as normal  making videos being active I celebrated  my 30th birthday on the 7th of March  with friends we went snowboarding and  surfing in the same day doing activities  and I felt completely normal and  present' on the 10th of March 20 2004 in  an Emirates flight from Los Angeles from  LAX that flew its way to Dubai and for  Dubai to Cape Town my reason for doing  this trip was to celebrate my wedding in  South Africa the following week now what  super important to note here is on  landing in Cape Town they screened every  single passenger that was on board  I got screened it's a little temperature  dial that they put up against Jafar yet  they read your temperature and if you  show symptoms they make you stay if not  they let you pass they screened me and  they let me pass I then went home I saw  my family I saw my parents I went on a  weekend away with really close friends  of mine to my bachelors where we were  all in very close proximity together we  then attended a big music festival in  Cape Town on the Sunday  but on the Monday I still hadn't got my  sense of taste or smell back then it  wasn't Tuesday the 17th of March where  other patients that have tested positive  for the clover 19 virus came out saying  that they have no sense of taste or  smell this all of a sudden immediately  urged me to go and get tested now in  South Africa we are really fortunate to  have an incredible testing facility it's  super simple to get tested you just have  to get a note from your doctor you go  down to the path care facility you hand  in your document and they give you a  swab and it takes about two to three  days for you to get your results and  that takes us to the 21st of March 2020  the day that I was supposed to get  married  we're obviously our wedding was  postponed and for the best reasons  possible been on that afternoon my  doctor phoned me and told me that I have  tested positive and I got these folks  now I have absolutely no idea what this  all means I have not shown any symptoms  since being ill in the states other than  of course the loss of taste and smell  which is really [ __ ] by the way did I  indeed get the virus when I was in the  States if so I just truly hoped that I  was passed and fix the stage by the time  I got on a plane and decided to fly back  to South Africa but there were eighteen  days between the time that I was feeling  ill and recovered and got into the plane  to get on to South African soil there  are just so many unanswered questions  right now and I'm in no way a medical  professional I'm just hoping that my  story can somehow help others out there  and in the meantime I am in isolation in  my house in Cape Town for the next 14  days with Gabby and with Joey come say  hi  just go say that about Joey hello guys  we are sending you all love and I'll  keep you posted with my symptoms moving  forwards but you know like I said  hopefully it's all in the past  I am isolated in my house and will do my  best to make creative videos while I'm  sitting here I'm sure that it's gonna  drive me insane 14 days well other than  that don't forget your awesome brew and  stay safe  [Music]
 

